when I show people my artwork in real life, I tend to emphasize the form, more
so than the fiction. As in, I describe how I made the thing, and not what the
thing is. Because that's how art works, the artist has their own interpretation
and the viewers get to decide how they feel about it.

I think I would be a lot more conventionally successful if I showed people the
thing and said "here's why the thing is important" but frankly I don't want to
have to explain myself. I just am, view me at your leisure.
